  N17_Idempotency [label="IDEMPOTENCY CHECKS BEFORE OUTPUT
================================
Before writing outputs:
- check whether a snapshot for the same manifest/target/context already exists
- if it exists and ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no, create a versioned snapshot or stop for confirmation
- same manifest plus same live state should produce same snapshot classification
- if live state changed, record the observed difference
- do not merge stale snapshots silently
- do not overwrite prior CONFIG_STATE_SNAPSHOT artifacts.

CIP04 may compare with a prior snapshot only as read-only evidence.", color="#F9A825", fillcolor="#FFFDE7"];
  N18_Safety [label="SAFE COMMANDS / FORBIDDEN ACTIONS
=================================
Allowed in CIP04 after confirmation:
- read provided manifest/request/spec/hook files
- read exact config policy files
- run read-only config status/list/show/help commands
- run lv inventory/status commands
- grep exact names in config.sh/installers.sh/steps/plans
- inspect target state marker directories without changing them
- produce snapshot artifacts.

Forbidden in CIP04:
- edit config files
- edit public tooling
- edit main DOT or CIP DOT files
- mutate private evidence or companion outputs
- run bootstrap step execution
- run mount, pull, push
- install packages or create envs
- read or print credential contents
- expire/remove/create accounts unless explicitly in later approved CIP06
- start Docker, Runpod, paid APIs, or live infra
- claim a planned change is safe to apply without CIP05/CIP06.", color="#BF360C", fillcolor="#FBE9E7"];
  N19_ResponseFormat [label="REQUIRED RESPONSE FORMAT
========================
Current phase: CIP04 live config-state resolution
Selected DOT:
Addressed role:
Variable block proposed/confirmed:
Source manifest read:
Source requests read:
Required source contract status:
Targets inspected:
Commands proposed/executed/skipped:
Config surfaces inspected:
Manifest item resolution summary:
Already covered:
Missing/conflicting/blocked:
Recommended CIP05 planning focus:
Outputs created/proposed:
Safety status:
Decision: PASS / STOP
Recommended next route:", color="#37474F", fillcolor="#ECEFF1"];
  N20_PassStop [label="PASS / STOP CONDITIONS
======================
PASS only if:
- variables confirmed
- manifest/request source status recorded
- ANX04/hook source contract applied or fallback noted
- read-only live inspection was explicitly allowed, or unavailable state was recorded honestly
- exact commands/file reads were proposed before execution
- config surfaces were inspected or marked unresolved
- manifest items were resolved into already-covered/missing/conflict/blocked/needs-plan classes
- CONFIG_STATE_SNAPSHOT.md/json contract satisfied or proposed
- no forbidden mutation occurred.

STOP if:
- user has not confirmed
- live inspection permission is not granted and no offline snapshot is available
- a command may mutate or is uncertain
- credentials would be read or printed
- requested action is config write, package install, bootstrap execution, mount/pull/push, live infra, public edit, DOT edit, evidence mutation, or destructive lifecycle
- output would overwrite existing artifact with ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no.

After PASS:
Do not silently run CIP05. Recommend CIP05 only when a CONFIG_INTEGRATION_PLAN should be generated.", color="#B71C1C", fillcolor="#FFEBEE"];
  N21_Reentry [label="RE-ENTRY INTO CIP AND V7 PIPELINE
=================================
If all manifest items are already covered, CIP04 may recommend CIP05 no-op planning or direct closeout planning, but must not skip the operator decision.

If items are missing, partial, conflicting, or blocked, the normal next route is CIP05 for CONFIG_INTEGRATION_PLAN generation.

If live inspection is blocked, return STOP with required operator action.

CIP04 does not replace skeleton/organ P lanes. It is the bridge between approved config-infra intent and live vmuser config-state truth.", color="#333333", fillcolor="#F5F5F5"];
